- B>W | take paid work as a casting office's reader, to be in the room every week | v: achievement, security | grants: contact in the trade | tribal: become the one who speaks the other parts when the elders hear new players | magic: get paid work as the reader at a company's trials, to be in the room every week | chance: 55
- R>U | go to every free workshop and late-night class in the city, out of pure hunger | habit | door | v: stimulation, achievement | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | tribal: sit at every fire where an old teller is teaching, out of pure hunger | magic: go to every open lesson and late class in the city, out of pure hunger | chance: 90
- G>B | ask your old youth theatre leader to put your name forward to anyone they know | v: tradition, achievement | tribal: ask the old teller of your own band to speak for you at other fires | magic: ask your old children's master to put your name forward to the companies he knows | chance: 55
works: A call comes at last: a small part and a few weeks' work, and {N} is an actor again.
works: {N} learns to live in the gaps: the day job, the classes, the self-tapes, and a life that goes on between them.
fails: The weeks turn into months, and {N} stops telling people at parties what {N} does.
fails: {partner} and {N} have the same argument about money for the third time, and nobody wins it.

