requires: in the threshold season of professional actor, within the first six months after taking the title: step 2, the season's transforming chance, when the first choices about the kind of work begin
likelier: an actor with two kinds of offer at once; an agent who asks for a plan; an actor who trained in one tradition and worked in another
rarer: an actor with no work at all that month; an older actor who came to it late and wants only to act
scene: Four months in, {N} sits for new photographs for the casting directory, and the form asks for one line beneath them: what kind of actor is this? {mentor}, an old actor from the first job, says over a drink that the next three choices will answer the question whether {N} does or not.
scene W: {N} thinks of the old hands on the first job: there every night, word-perfect, holding the show together without anyone noticing.
scene U: {N} thinks of the parts that frighten {N}, the great old plays, and the years of work it would take to be ready for them.
scene B: {N} looks at the careers {N} admires and sees the pattern: the right agent, the right parts, a plan, and no time wasted.
scene R: {N} wants the rush of the first night again and again: the big part, the risk. Nothing else feels like being alive.
scene G: {N} thinks of the theatre in the home town, of the people there who would come every season, and of acting as something that belongs to a place.
scene tribal: Four moons in, the elders ask {N} at the fire what kind of teller-player {N} means to be. The band will remember the answer.
scene magic: Four months in, the brokers' roll asks for a line beneath {Ns} name, and an old player of the company asks over wine what kind of player {N} means to be.
- W | be the company player: word-perfect, there every night, ready for whatever the show needs | identity | v: conformity, benevolence | tribal: be the band's steady teller: word-perfect, there every night, ready for whatever the telling needs | magic: be the company's steady player: word-perfect, there every night, ready for any part | chance: 82
- U | train for the great parts: a class every week for years, voice, text and body | identity | binds | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | tribal: train for the great tellings: every voice and every dance, every day for years | magic: train for the great parts of the old plays with a master of voice, for years | chance: 70
- B | build a career with a plan: the right agent, the right parts, nothing beneath it | identity | v: achievement, power | tribal: plan a road to the great mask: the right elders, the right tellings, nothing beneath it | magic: plan a road to the court playhouse: the right broker, the right parts, nothing beneath it | chance: 70
- R | chase the frightening parts, and never take the safe one | identity | v: stimulation | tribal: ask for the tellings that frighten the others, and never take the safe part | chance: 68
- G | go back to the theatre of your home region, and become its actor | identity | binds | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: came home | tribal: go back to your own band, and become its teller-player for good | magic: go back to the playhouse of your home town, and become its player | chance: 45
- W>G | join a touring company that takes plays to towns that never see one | identity | binds | v: universalism, benevolence | tribal: walk with the tellers who carry the old stories to the small bands of the hills | magic: join a wagon company that plays the villages no licensed company visits | chance: 60
- U>W | specialise in the old verse plays, and learn their rules line by line | identity | v: achievement, conformity | tribal: learn the oldest tellings word for word, as the band has always kept them | magic: specialise in the old verse plays of the realm, and learn their rules line by line | chance: 78
- B>U | sign with an agent for adverts and company films, and pay for training with it | identity | binds | v: achievement, security | tribal: promise to play at every feast a rich family gives, and trade the gifts for lessons with the best teller | magic: sign with a broker for the mirror-plays of the great houses, and pay a master of voice with it | chance: 70
- R>B | throw everything at one big audition season, and make your name or quit | identity | binds | v: achievement, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | tribal: throw everything at the summer gathering, to be seen by every band or go back to the hunt | magic: throw everything at the court season's trials, to make your name or go home | chance: 35
- G>R | act wherever the road leads, with whoever is there, for the joy of it | identity | v: hedonism, self-direction | tribal: play wherever the band camps, with whoever is at the fire, for the joy of it | chance: 85
works: The answer holds: within weeks the next choices fall into line, and the work starts to look like a road.
works: {mentor} hears what {N} chose and raises a glass to it.
fails: {N} writes three different lines under the photographs and deletes them all, and the next job decides for {N}.
fails: The choice is made, the first door it needs stays shut, and {N} wonders whether it was the wrong one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 81. step 3 (cycle s1)

== half a year on, still an actor
tier: inner
threshold: title:professional actor
step: 3
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-100
times: per new professional actor: once, about five months in, near the end of the threshold season; about 4 lives in 1,000 (catalogue share)
holds: professional actor
stakes: .8
tone: joy
life: work, friends, family
horizon: months
roles: friend, partner, colleague
earth: five months in and still an actor: friends from before ask when you will be on television, a partner sees you between jobs, and a company has become a second family
tribal: five moons in and still a teller-player: the hunters you grew up with tease you at the river, and the tellers' fire has become a second hearth
magic: five months in and still a player: old friends ask when you will play at court, and the company has become a second family on the road
requires: in the threshold season of professional actor, within the first six months after taking the title: step 3, near the end of the six months, when the first months as an actor have settled into a life
likelier: an actor with a partner or a family from before; old friends outside the trade; a few jobs behind them
rarer: an actor who has worked without a break; an actor from a family of actors
scene: Five months on, {N} is still an actor, just: a second job, a few days on a series, and a lot of waiting in between. At a wedding {friend} introduces {N} as "the actor", and everyone asks the same two questions: what has {N} been in, and has {N} met anyone famous? {partner} has learned the timetable of a working actor: weeks of nothing, then weeks of never being home.
scene W: {N} has found the rhythm: the day job's rota, the class on Tuesdays, self-tapes on Sundays, the union subscription paid on time.
scene U: {N} has started to notice what {N} does better than six months ago, and what has not changed at all.
scene B: {N} counts what the first months have brought: two credits, a few contacts, a casting director who remembers {Ns} name. A beginning.
scene R: {N} is tired of explaining at weddings what an actor does all week, and longs for the next first night.
scene G: The old friends from home have not changed, and {N} has, a little. Some evenings that is a comfort, and some evenings it is not.
scene tribal: Five moons on, the hunters {N} grew up with tease {N} at the river about the tellers' soft hands, and the tellers' fire has become a second hearth.
scene magic: Five months on, old friends in the lane ask when {N} will play at court, and the company has become a second family on the road.
- W | pay the union subscription, keep a diary, and treat acting as a proper job | v: conformity, security | grants: union card | tribal: take your place among the band's tellers before the elders, and keep its customs | magic: pay your dues to the players' guild, and keep your token bright | chance: 90
- U | write down what you can do now that you could not six months ago | v: achievement, self-direction | tribal: go over by the fire what you can do now that you could not five moons ago | chance: 95
- B | follow up every contact from the half-year with a note and a new photograph | habit | v: power, achievement | self_control: + | tribal: send a small gift to every teller and elder who praised your telling this winter | magic: send a note and a new likeness to every master and broker you met this season | chance: 85
- R | answer the questions at the wedding with a wild story, and dance till they close | v: hedonism, stimulation | tribal: answer the hunters' teasing with a wild telling of your own, and dance till the fire dies | magic: answer the questions at the feast with a tall tale, and dance till the tavern closes | chance: 94
- G | keep Sunday dinner with the family, whatever job you are in | habit | v: tradition, benevolence | self_control: + | tribal: eat at your mother's hearth every few days, whatever telling you are in | magic: keep the rest-day meal with your family, whatever company you are with | chance: 60
- W>U | go to class every Tuesday, even in the weeks when there is work | v: conformity, achievement | tribal: sit with the old teller every few nights, even when you are in a telling | magic: go to the guild's lesson every week, even when you are in a play | chance: 65
- U>B | work out which castings led to work, and spend your time only on those | v: achievement, power | tribal: work out which tellings brought gifts, and give your days only to those | magic: work out which trials led to a part, and spend your coin only on those | chance: 75
- B>R | spend the fee from the last job on a week away with your partner | v: hedonism, power | tribal: trade the winter's gifts for a feast with your partner | magic: spend the season's wages on a week by the sea with your partner | chance: 90
- R>G | bring your new actor friends home to meet the old ones, and see what happens | v: benevolence, stimulation | mark: made a friend | tribal: bring the tellers to your own band's fire, and let the two worlds meet | magic: bring the company to the old tavern in your lane, and let the two worlds meet | chance: 75
- G>W | go back to your old youth theatre, and run a free workshop for the children | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: go back to the children of your own band, and teach them the small spirits' parts | magic: go back to the guild's children's company, and teach them a free lesson | chance: 90
works: Half a year in, {N} can say "I'm an actor" without looking at the floor.
works: {partner} comes to see the small part in the latest show, and cheers at the curtain call.
fails: The half-year ends with more waiting than working, and {N} counts the money twice a week.
fails: An old friend says, not unkindly, that {N} has changed, and {N} cannot say they are wrong.

